# Requests for the IDE HTTP client (Visual Studio, Rider, VS Code REST Client).
# docker compose exposes the API on 8080; `dotnet run` uses 5080.
@api = http://localhost:8080
# Paste the keys from your .env (never commit real keys here).
@publisherKey = PUBLISHER_API_KEY-from-.env
@adminKey = ADMIN_API_KEY-from-.env

### Health
GET {{api}}/health

### Create a subscription (the secret is returned only here)
# The sample receiver does not know this generated secret and answers 401, so these deliveries end up
# Failed with "http_401": the expected reaction to a signature the subscriber cannot verify.
POST {{api}}/subscriptions
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "manual: Contoso Air delays",
  "eventTypes": ["flight.delayed"],
  "filter": { "airline": "CT" },
  "webhookUrl": "http://webhook-receiver:8080/webhooks/manual"
}

### Rejected: host is not on the allowlist
POST {{api}}/subscriptions
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "should fail",
  "eventTypes": ["flight.*"],
  "webhookUrl": "http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/"
}

### List subscriptions (no secrets)
GET {{api}}/subscriptions
X-Api-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Forbidden: a publisher key cannot manage subscriptions (403)
GET {{api}}/subscriptions
X-Api-Key: {{publisherKey}}

### Unauthorized: no key (401)
GET {{api}}/subscriptions

### Publish an event (send it twice: the second answer is 200 with "duplicate": true)
POST {{api}}/events
X-Api-Key: {{publisherKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "0b9f5bb5-61c1-4bd4-8b52-7a1c0c3b5d11",
  "type": "flight.delayed",
  "source": "manual",
  "attributes": { "airline": "CT", "flightNumber": "CT101", "origin": "NTH", "destination": "STH" },
  "data": { "delayMinutes": 40, "reason": "Late inbound aircraft" }
}

### Delivery status of that event
# The receiver's own subscriptions succeed; the one created above fails with "http_401" (see there).
GET {{api}}/events/0b9f5bb5-61c1-4bd4-8b52-7a1c0c3b5d11/deliveries
X-Api-Key: {{publisherKey}}
